cmprovision4 (1.6.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Runs on WLAN Pi OS 26.10: the nginx site is enabled as cmprovision.conf,
    since WLAN Pi OS loads only sites-enabled/*.conf; existing installations
    get the new link name on upgrade. The installation warns when another
    TFTP server holds UDP port 69 (WLAN Pi OS runs tftpd-hpa), which keeps
    modules from network booting.
  * cmprovision-restore --data-only moves the data to a new system: the
    database, .env (APP_KEY), the firmware store, the uploaded images and
    the dnsmasq config, without the old system's nginx, PHP and network
    configuration.
  * Checked as the production provisioner on Raspberry Pi OS 13 (trixie)
    with PHP 8.4 and NetworkManager: data moved from Debian 11 with
    --data-only, network boot, provisioning and Telegram notifications.

 -- nimbo78 <igor.sin.78@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:07:29 +0300

cmprovision4 (1.6.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * LEDs show where a module is: in progress ACT blinks fast with PWR on,
    done ACT and PWR take turns fading in and out, failed ACT is dim while
    PWR double-flashes. Fading and dimming come from a small helper the
    module downloads (public/tools/ledpattern); without it kernel triggers
    show the same states. Refusals and server errors show the failed state
    too.
  * ACT works during provisioning: it shares its pin with the SPI bus of the
    EEPROM, and the LED driver now takes it back after the pre-install
    scripts. Before, ACT stayed dark and the end of a run blinked PWR only.
  * Identify: a module that finished keeps asking the server whether to
    blink; the Identify button on the module card and the dashboard makes
    it alternate its LEDs for 30 seconds, Stop ends that sooner.

 -- nimbo78 <igor.sin.78@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:21:47 +0300

cmprovision4 (1.6.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * EEPROM before and after: every module reports its running bootloader
    (version and settings) before the pre-install scripts, and the flash
    script tells whether flashrom wrote the EEPROM or found it identical.
    The completion notification shows the change.
  * Module card (/cms/<serial>, linked from the dashboard and the CMs list)
    instead of the View dialog: the steps of the last run with start,
    duration and speed, the bootloader before and after with changed
    settings marked, the script logs and the module's history. A failed or
    silent module shows the step where it stopped and what to do about it,
    for every kind of failure.

