cmprovision4 (1.6.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: postinst never follows symlinks in places the web user can
    write to. Since 1.6.5 a compromised web process could put a symlink in
    place of storage/app/upload-tmp and be handed its target, any root-owned
    directory, on the next package upgrade.
  * Security: stored secrets (Mattermost bot token, SNMP community, SNMPv3
    passwords) are only used for the address they were saved with; a new
    address needs them entered again.
  * The code belongs to root; the web server writes only to storage,
    bootstrap/cache, public/uploads, etc, the database directory and .env.
    Existing installations are converted on upgrade.
  * Dashboard: the log refreshes itself, shows the date of older entries and
    names the time zone.
  * Message boxes are in colour again (CSS rebuilt, Tailwind 1 leftovers
    replaced); the browser tab shows an icon.
  * Packaging: debhelper compat 13; services are restarted after an upgrade
    instead of being stopped before it.

 -- nimbo78 <igor.sin.78@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:52:28 +0300

cmprovision4 (1.6.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Live progress of every module on the dashboard: step, progress bar with
    percent, speed and time left while the image is written and verified,
    total time, failure reason with where it stopped, and a warning when a
    module stops reporting. Modules report sectors from /sys/block every
    5 seconds, best effort; rows stay in port order.
  * Notifications, set up on the settings page: Mattermost and Telegram
    bots keep a thread per batch of modules (a summary edited on every
    event, a reply per module); Mattermost/Slack incoming webhooks and JSON
    webhooks get a message per event. Sent after the module got its answer;
    errors show on the channel.
  * Ethernet switch on the settings page: SNMP v2c or v3, lookup method,
    Test button with port, MAC, VLAN and module, hints per vendor. The port
    lookup reads Q-BRIDGE-MIB, BRIDGE-MIB (bridge ports mapped by
    HUAWEI-L2IF-MIB where needed), HUAWEI-L2MAM-MIB and Cisco IOS per-VLAN
    instances, prefers the access port over an uplink, shows port
    descriptions and remembers the method that worked. SNMPv3 VLAN contexts
    work around php-snmp keeping a pointer to a freed context name.
  * Raspberry Pi OS Trixie (Debian 13, PHP 8.4): composer.lock installs
    (league/commonmark pinned to 1.6), packages built there own the
    application files as www-data again (Rules-Requires-Root), and times
    are shown in the system time zone read from the OS.

 -- nimbo78 <igor.sin.78@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:58:25 +0300

cmprovision4 (1.6.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * EEPROM firmware download works again: images come from the
    firmware-2711 default/latest channels on GitHub (only missing files,
    checksum verified) and from the rpi-eeprom package; new artisan
    command firmware:update. (upstream #43)
  * Image upload shows progress, speed and remaining time, can be
    cancelled and reports errors; the Images page refreshes itself while
    the SHA256 is being computed.
  * Image write failures are explained in the web log (curl exit code,
    decompressor errors, diagnosis); nginx no longer drops slow downloads
    (send_timeout 6h for /uploads/, added to existing installations);
    a failed write clears the partition table so the module net-boots
    again; module reports are retried for up to 10 minutes instead of
    being lost. (upstream #59, #44)
  * /scriptexecute never answers with an error page: an unreachable SNMP
    switch, internal errors and a deleted project go to the web log.
  * Project activation (EEPROM image build) is shared by the web UI and
    the API, with settings normalised and the firmware path allowlisted.
  * Settings: deleting a static IP updates dnsmasq.conf; hostnames are
    written correctly.
  * Images page tolerates missing files; timestamps shown in the server's
    time zone (storage stays UTC); upload_tmp_dir kept on disk (Debian 13
    has /tmp in RAM); production defaults in .env; [pi4] in config.txt so
    EEPROM flashing also works on a Pi 4. (upstream #24, #40, #41)
  * Upgrades restart php-fpm, so opcache does not keep serving the code of
    the previous version.
  * API: project scripts readable and changeable, script CRUD. (#55)
  * Ships public/uploads (#28) and the cmprovision-backup /
    cmprovision-restore commands; phpunit is no longer installed on the
    server (it was a production dependency);
    Docker test bench; README for NetworkManager-based Raspberry Pi OS.

 -- nimbo78 <igor.sin.78@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 08:20:57 +0300

